cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use cgiarGenomics, please cite it as below. When you run it through Bioflow, cite Bioflow as well."
type: software
title: "cgiarGenomics. Reading, quality control and imputation of SNP marker data"
abstract: >-
  cgiarGenomics reads bi-allelic SNP marker data from hapmap, VCF, DArTSeq and
  DArTag files for diploid and polyploid crops, and converts them to allele
  dosages in an adegenet genlight object. It provides quality metrics,
  sequential filtering of loci and individuals, imputation by allele frequency,
  Random Forest or Beagle, merging of replicate samples, identity-by-state and
  Mendelian checks, and export to VCF. It is the genomic data engine of
  Bioflow, the CGIAR breeding analytics pipeline.
authors:
  - given-names: "Sergio Andres"
    family-names: "Cruz"
    email: "s.cruz@cgiar.org"
  - given-names: "Lorena"
    family-names: "Guimarães Batista"
version: "1.0.3"
license: MIT
